            <ArticleTitle>An unusual finding in the inguinal canal of a 26-week pregnant patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10029-012-0958-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inguinal herniae are a common pathology found in both paediatric and adult populations. The presence of bowel in the hernia sac is anticipated; however, occasionally other structures may be found within the sac. We describe a case of a leiomyoma that had undergone red degeneration in the inguinal canal of a 26-week pregnant female. With this case report, we hope to expand the diagnostic paradigm in the setting of a painful swelling in the inguinal canal of a pregnant female.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
